+//   pass at full rate: how much shading the game meant to save is unknown (no count in that journal). Counted at recording, per command buffer: the binds and unbinds, the render
+//   targets set while one is bound and the pixels of their first target (or depth), the palettes and the palette mode; tsummary prints it every 300 frames while any were seen. Only a
+//   count: mapping the rate image to a Metal rasterization rate map changes the screen's geometry (physical and logical coordinates, a resample after) and is not done
+static pthread_mutex_t g_rb_sri_mu = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+static struct { const void *cmd; } g_rb_sri[16]; static _Atomic int g_rb_sri_n;   // command buffers recording with a shading-rate image bound (g_rb_sri_mu; more than 16 are not counted)
